&lt;h2&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Scale Ecosystem Sales Manager - Europe, Middle East, and Africa (EMEA), you&#39;ll help fuel GitLab&#39;s growth by turning our emerging partner ecosystem into a consistent, scalable source of new customers. Based in the UK, with Dublin also considered, you&#39;ll focus on partner-sourced Scale pipeline generation through repeatable partner-led campaigns, systematic account mapping, and whitespace analysis. You&#39;ll work with Scale Account Executives, Field Marketing, regional sales leadership, distributors, long-tail resellers, and hyperscalers such as Amazon Web Services (AWS) and Google Cloud to integrate partners throughout the sales cycle and accelerate marketplace transactions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll own programmatic partner engagement across your territory, from identifying and recruiting partners to enabling and activating them at scale. Your work will support GitLab&#39;s Scale growth targets by building a measurable, partner-led demand engine through event strategies, one-to-many campaigns, partner portals, and automated systems. You&#39;ll also contribute to business planning, pipeline forecasting, and clear reporting on partner impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Drive partner-sourced Scale pipeline generation through scalable partner programs, campaigns, and systematic account mapping.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Collaborate with Scale Account Executives, Field Marketing, and regional sales leaders to integrate partners into territory planning and demand generation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Execute repeatable partner-led campaigns aligned with regional territories, including industry plays, account blitzes, and market-specific roadshows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Identify whitespace and map accounts with partners to surface new customer opportunities and expand first-order reach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;Identify, recruit, and build programmatic relationships with emerging partners, distributors, long-tail resellers, and hyperscalers such as AWS and Google Cloud.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;6&quot;&gt;Support partner enablement and activation, including hyperscaler co-sell and marketplace acceleration initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;7&quot;&gt;Execute event-driven partner strategies, including partner alignment before events, lead capture during events, and pipeline conversion after events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;8&quot;&gt;Manage one-to-many partner engagement through partner portals and automated systems, providing weekly forecasts and reports that track partner-sourced pipeline, campaign performance, and territory impact against regional Scale growth targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Experience in business-to-business sales development, business development, or partner-driven pipeline generation, including identifying and recruiting ecosystem partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Familiarity with partner ecosystems and programmatic demand generation involving distributors, long-tail resellers, and hyperscalers such as AWS and Google Cloud.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Ability to design, execute, and improve scalable demand generation approaches, including one-to-many partner engagement and event-driven campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Experience using Salesforce and sales development or marketing automation tools to manage, forecast, and report on partner-sourced pipeline and campaign performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;Analytical skills to interpret campaign results, partner activation metrics, and territory impact, then turn those insights into clear plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;6&quot;&gt;Clear written and verbal communication skills and the ability to collaborate with account executives, Field Marketing, and regional sales leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;7&quot;&gt;Fluency in English. German, French, or Spanish language skills are a strong plus for this EMEA-wide role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;8&quot;&gt;Interest in GitLab, open source software, and modern software development practices, with openness to travel and to applying transferable experience from sales, partnerships, or digital marketing in a remote, results-focused environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
